 **Parameters and Typical Values:**
-*   `k` (Softness/Sharpness): Controls the width of the penumbra. Higher values produce sharper shadows (narrower penumbra), lower values produce softer shadows (wider penumbra) [S6, unofficial]. Typical values range from $4.0$ to $32.0$ [S7, S8, S13, unofficial].
+*   `k` (Softness/Sharpness): Controls the width of the penumbra. Higher values produce sharper shadows (narrower penumbra), lower values produce softer shadows (wider penumbra) [S6, unofficial]. Typical values range from $4.0$ to $32.0$ [S7, S8, S13, unofficial]. Some implementations parameterize softness via light radius $L_{size}$, where $k = 1/L_{size}$ (e.g., $L_{size} = 0.03$) [S6, unofficial].
 *   `minDist` (Start Offset): Prevents the ray from starting inside the surface. Typical value: $0.01$ [S4, unofficial].
